From: helmfile-enhancement-plan
Subject: [PATCH] PR-T-08 — Replace KEDA TCP test with gRPC health-check probe

Closes G8 (KEDA test is TCP-only).
Branch: fix/keda-test-actual-grpc

The current job uses `nc -zv ... 7233` which only verifies a TCP socket
opens — exactly the failure mode that DOES still happen even when
KEDA's gRPC scaler is broken (HF-10). This patch swaps the image to
fullstorydev/grpcurl and asserts the response includes
"status": "SERVING".

Critical: pin the image (no :latest); tied to PR-T-12 ban.

---
 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-temporal-connectivity-job.yaml | 14 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-temporal-connectivity-job.yaml b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-temporal-connectivity-job.yaml
--- a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-temporal-connectivity-job.yaml
+++ b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/test-keda-temporal-connectivity-job.yaml
@@ -16,12 +16,20 @@ spec:
       restartPolicy: Never
       containers:
         - name: probe
-          image: curlimages/curl:latest
+          image: fullstorydev/grpcurl:v1.9.1-alpine
           command:
             - /bin/sh
             - -c
             - |
-              nc -zv temporal-frontend.temporal.svc.cluster.local 7233
+              set -euo pipefail
+              echo "[1/3] DNS lookup..."
+              nslookup temporal-frontend.temporal.svc.cluster.local
+              echo "[2/3] gRPC health check..."
+              OUT=$(grpcurl -plaintext -connect-timeout 5 -max-time 10 \
+                temporal-frontend.temporal.svc.cluster.local:7233 \
+                grpc.health.v1.Health/Check)
+              echo "${OUT}"
+              echo "[3/3] Asserting SERVING..."
+              echo "${OUT}" | grep -q '"status": "SERVING"' \
+                || { echo "FAIL: gRPC health is NOT SERVING (HF-10 / G8)"; exit 1; }
+              echo "OK"
       backoffLimit: 1
       activeDeadlineSeconds: 60
